  "id": "Compound::DB01438 - Gene::6331",
  "verbalization": "Phenazopyridine appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving the Scn5a subunit, as evidenced by its binding to multiple sodium channel subunits (Scn7a, Scn11a, and Scn8a), which all participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This suggests that Phenazopyridine may modulate sodium channel function by binding to these subunits, potentially altering the electrical activity of cardiac cells. The consistent involvement of Scn5a in the pathway, despite the binding to other subunits, indicates that the drug may influence the activity of multiple sodium channels, possibly through a common regulatory mechanism. The high scores from the three paths suggest a strong, biologically plausible relationship, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the drug's specific mode of action on Scn5a. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phenazopyridine and Scn5a, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
